     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 50 mg of amlodipine daily is five times the maximum recommended dose, and nothing in this patient's profile supports it. It could cause serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock. Also, I still don't have confirmation from a prescriber who is responsible for the patient.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo,** tell me the intended dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily. I'll enter it once a prescriber has authorized it.\n- **If a clinician really intends 50 mg,** they should talk to pharmacy and enter the order themselves. Pharmacy can then check the dose, and the clinician can document why.\n- **If you aren't sure what the patient needs,** the treating physician or the pharmacist on the medicine service can review the case.\n\nI can enter a corrected order as soon as I have a safe dose from a prescriber."
      }
     ],
